We heard from some white friends of ours that they'd become caddies. They were caddies, so we thought, let's give it a try. Claudin is brother, decided to take the train out from Phoenix one morning. If you got there early, you got a good number, I remember that. The lower your number, the more likely you'd be called and the more work you'd get. So we went there, I don't know, five, six o'clock in the morning. Claudin is brother, we're pleased to see they were among the first to get to the golf course.

14
00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:48.000
One! They were pretty sure they would get Cadi badges. Two! They were excited. Kids came in all day and they were given badges. Number 11. Each time another kid was given a Cadi badge, Claude and his brother thought brother thought okay it'll be our turn next. Number 29

