Claude graduated and became a psychology professor. Over the following 20 years, he studied the nature of alcohol addiction. But his experiences growing up and in graduate school stayed with him. He didn't yet have a conceptual framework to explain them. They just felt like personal experiences. And then, while he was at the University of Michigan, he noticed something about his students that prompted him to make a connection with his own life. African American students at the University of Michigan

