ability, how smart I am. Then that stereotype about my group is relevant. I can't ignore it in interpreting my experience of taking a test. This is a hard test. It's important to me. I'm going to be worried that as I experience frustration on it, that I'm confirming the stereotype or that I'm going to be seen to confirm the stereotype. That all that extra worry, take up cognitive resources, undermines performance, that's what happened. Black students equally skilled to white students didn't do as well

57
